# ── Old Webflow site (the crystalarc.net still live today) ──
# Its sitemap carries 528 URLs. The blog block above already maps 56 of them
# because those slugs were migrated intact. The rest had no rule at all and
# would have 404'd the moment the domain is cut over, taking whatever ranking
# and inbound links they hold with them. A 301 to the nearest equivalent page
# passes that signal on; a 404 discards it.
#
# The old structure is a Webflow CMS with one page per SKU, so there is no
# like-for-like target for those — the new site has four category pages, not
# 429 product pages. They all go to /en/products, which is the honest nearest
# equivalent and beats a dead end for anyone arriving on an old link.
#
# /gifts is also indexed with pagination query strings (?9dd2465a_page=2…26).
# Netlify matches on path only, so the single rule covers all of them.
